## 6. Kill gates, cheapest first

Hardware assumed: one 48 GB GPU (RTX A6000) with host RAM of at least 64 GB, plus the owner's work server. Models: Qwen3-4B for fast iteration, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct for comparability with the kvpress leaderboard and with ShadowKV/Fathom.

**K0 — equivalence (minutes, any GPU).** Implement the prefix-closed scorer in HF with chunked prefill. Run on a prompt P and on P + X. Finalized keep-masks must match byte for byte. Then simulate a cache hit (store P's compressed blocks and dense tail, resume on X) and a miss (prefill P + X from scratch): suffix logits must be equal up to bf16 reordering (report max abs diff; expect ~1e-3 or less). Watch for floating-point ties flipping a per-block top-k; compute block decisions in one canonical pass with deterministic kernels, or break ties by position.

**I0 — index quality, offline (~1 GPU-hour).** Capture pre-RoPE keys and held-out queries from 20 long-context prompts (RULER 16K/32K, plus 5 context-intensive prompts per 2604.08426's task types). For PCA (Loki), CrossCov-U and SAKI at ranks 16/32/64, compute recall-at-k for k in {64, 256, 1024} and bytes-to-reach-95%-recall. Pass: CrossCov-U cuts bytes by 15-20% at matched recall versus PCA. If it ties SAKI, adopt SAKI's projection as the baseline and make the runtime the contribution.

**K1 — eviction quality (10-20 GPU-hours).** Qwen3-4B and Llama-3.1-8B at 2x, 4x, 8x on RULER (4K, 16K), LongBench and SCBench shared-context tasks, through kvpress with the query excluded. Compare prefix-closed v1 (several L, both scorers) against dense-then-compress SnapKV, KVzip, Expected Attention, KVzap. Pass: within about 2 points of the best baseline at 4x. Also sweep needle position within the block to check for phase effects (Periodic Weak Spots, 2609.36322, found up to 40-point gaps from fixed chunk boundaries); if a gap appears, score each token from its own window [i+1, i+L], which stays prefix-closed. Fail: publish the "price of closure" curve as a short analysis.

**K2 — sharing value (CPU plus a few GPU-hours).** Replay multi-request traces (SCBench, multi-turn chat, agent trajectories) and compute hit rate and memory per request for: no compression; compaction eviction; IntentKV-style masking; prefix-closed compression; and the index-only design. Pass: clear memory-per-request win at matched hit rate.

**I1 — offloaded decode (~10 GPU-hours).** Build the index-plus-offload path in HF first (host-pinned KV pages, GPU index, group-shared selection, page fetch). Measure accuracy versus bytes transferred per step and decode latency at 64K and 128K context, batch 1 and 8, for PCA index, CrossCov-U index, SAKI index, and a dense baseline. Include the context-intensive tasks. Pass: CrossCov-U index reaches the dense baseline's accuracy with fewer bytes per step than PCA, and the end-to-end decode at 128K is faster than dense on the same GPU.

**K3 — engine (2-3 weeks of engineering, ~10 GPU-hours).** SGLang radix cache storing finalized compressed blocks and index blocks; throughput and latency on an 8B model under shared-prefix workloads. A junior can own this once K0-K2 and I0-I1 pass.

