## 7. Implementation plan for Claude Code

Repository layout (new repo, reuse code from `neymankv` by copying the capture, kvpress pipeline and stats modules):
```
sharekv/
  closure/      # block finalization, lookahead scoring, head-uniform selection, masked prefill, hit/miss simulator
  index/        # CrossCov-U, PCA, SAKI projections; calibration; group-shared selection; selection reuse
  offload/      # host-pinned KV pages, fetch scheduler, bytes accounting
  capture/      # hooks (pre/post-RoPE keys, values, queries, positions)
  eval/         # kvpress pipeline, RULER/LongBench/SCBench, paired bootstrap
  tests/        # synthetic tests, run before any GPU job
  runs/         # configs, CSVs, REPORT.md per phase, provenance (git commit, pip freeze, GPU, seeds, GPU-hours)
```
Synthetic tests before any GPU job: full-budget identity (no eviction reproduces full attention); prefix-closure on random tensors (masks for P equal masks for P+X); hit-equals-miss on random tensors; index recall sanity (rank d reproduces exact top-k); offload path correctness (fetched attention equals dense attention when everything is fetched).

Harness rules learned the hard way in the previous project: read tokenizers from `tokenizer.json` and assert a round-trip of "Hello world" (transformers 5.7 drops spaces for some models); use SDPA, not bf16 eager attention (it rounds scores before the softmax); match evaluation samples on task, question and answer, never on a salted hash; log kept-set sizes per head to verify budgets; never report differences without paired bootstrap intervals (differences under 8 points were noise throughout the previous project).

Order of work: K0 and the synthetic tests (day 1); I0 (day 1-2); K1 and I1 in parallel (week 1-2); K2 (week 2); decide; K3 (weeks 3-5).

