## 9. What not to do
- Do not evaluate piece 1 above 4x and expect it to compete with query-aware methods; the floor is proven.
- Do not benchmark the index on a GPU-resident cache; the speedup only exists when offloaded.
- Do not skip the context-intensive tasks; low-rank keys are known to fail there.
- Do not write the theory claim before searching vLLM, SGLang and TensorRT-LLM PRs for an existing threshold-eviction-plus-prefix-caching integration.

